+# Aegis — Production Ready Unified Patch
+
+This patch (aegis-production-ready-2026-02-13.patch) focuses on Phase 1-4 to move Aegis to production readiness:
+- Terraform (AWS) to provision S3 and KMS for object storage and Vault auto-unseal
+- Helm install helper and k8s values to deploy Vault with AWS KMS auto-unseal
+- Migration helper to move cosign keys into Vault KV/Transit
+- CI example showing where to integrate Vault-backed signing (replace with OIDC/Vault Agent in prod)
+- Vault-backed receipt_signer and encrypt_store implementations
+- Gatekeeper audit collection and flip-to-enforce scripts
+- Prometheus rules, ServiceMonitor and Alertmanager config for observability and alerting
+- Edge resilience tooling (sync retry, offline drill)
+- Federated orchestrator prototype with DP noise
+- DP utility functions
+
+Operator next steps (high level):
+1. Run Terraform to provision S3 and KMS, note outputs (bucket, KMS key id).
+2. Run tools/install_vault_helm_aws.sh <namespace> <release> <kms_key_id>, then initialize/unseal or configure auto-unseal per HashiCorp docs.
+3. Create Vault policies for transit and kv; create Kubernetes auth role and bind to ServiceAccounts for signing/encryption services.
+4. Migrate cosign keys using tools/migrate_cosign_to_vault.sh and/or create transit keys for signing.
+5. Replace CI signing placeholder with an ephemeral-signer that calls Vault Transit, or deploy a signing service that does the signing on behalf of CI (recommended: use short-lived OIDC tokens + Vault).
+6. Deploy Gatekeeper templates and run tools/gatekeeper_audit_to_mcp.py regularly; remediate violations and use tools/flip_gatekeeper_to_enforce.sh after audit window.
+7. Deploy Prometheus/Alertmanager and import prometheus rules and dashboards; configure Alertmanager receivers for oncall.
+8. Deploy edge sync_retry and run offline drills (tools/edge_offline_drill.sh).
+9. Harden federated orchestrator: add enrollment, authentication, secure aggregation and vetted DP library; validate utility on controlled pilot.
+
+Security note:
+- Do NOT keep VAULT_TOKEN in source or CI secrets. Prefer GitHub OIDC and Vault Kubernetes auth or Vault Agent with CSI secrets.
+- Pin KMS policies and S3 bucket policies to least privilege.
+
